<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Serbs</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Serbs are a South Slavic people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, predominantly <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christian. Large Serb communities lived within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, especially in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vojvodina">Vojvodina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>. The Austro-Hungarian Empire profile lists them among the nationalities of the multinational empire, and Serb nationalism was a major source of tension before 1914.</p></div>
